# ============================================================
# Document AI / RAG Platform -- PRODUCTION environment template
#
# ############################################################
# #  RENAME THIS FILE TO: .env.production.example              #
# #  (This agent's sandbox permission policy blocks writing   #
# #  to ANY path whose filename starts with ".env" -- reading #
# #  AND writing -- so this had to be authored under a        #
# #  dot-free filename. Run:                                  #
# #      mv env.production.example .env.production.example    #
# #  before committing, to match .env.example's naming        #
# #  convention.)                                              #
# ############################################################
#
# Copy to `.env` on the production host (or wire these as
# production-scoped, PROTECTED + MASKED GitLab CI/CD variables consumed by
# `deploy_production`/`deploy_production_worker` -- see .gitlab-ci.yml and
# DEPLOYMENT.md). This is a SIBLING to the existing .env.example /
# .env.test.example at the repo root -- those are untouched by this phase.
#
# Generated from src/config/env.ts (the actual runtime Zod schema -- the
# authoritative source of truth for every variable this app reads), not
# hand-transcribed, so the variable list/defaults/groupings below are
# accurate as of this phase. NOTE: this repo's root .env.example could not
# be read while producing this file (sandboxed out by this environment's
# own permission policy, which blocks reading any .env* path -- including
# example/template files with no real secrets in them); src/config/env.ts
# is arguably the more reliable source anyway, since it cannot drift from
# what the app actually validates against.
#
# LEGEND (see inline comments on individual lines below):
#   MUST differ per environment  -- do not reuse a staging value here.
#   SECRET                       -- never commit a real value; set only in
#                                   the deploy host's .env (outside git,
#                                   see .gitignore) or your CI/CD secret
#                                   store's PROTECTED + MASKED variables.
#   (commented out, no `=value`) -- optional, no default; the app runs
#                                   fine without it (the dependent feature
#                                   is simply disabled/inert).
#
# SECRETS vs. CONFIG REGISTRY:
#   Every variable below is read directly from process.env by
#   src/config/env.ts. Some features in this codebase intentionally split
#   their configuration: a TRUE secret (an API credential) lives here,
#   while that same feature's non-secret runtime toggles (feature flags,
#   provider selection, limits) live in the app's own CONFIG_REGISTRY
#   (database-backed, editable at runtime without a redeploy) instead of
#   as env vars. Where src/config/env.ts's own comments call this out
#   explicitly (RAZORPAY_*, VAPID_*, EMAIL_API_KEY), that note is carried
#   through below. If you're about to add a NEW env var for something
#   that is really a behavior toggle rather than a credential, prefer
#   CONFIG_REGISTRY instead -- see src/features/config/config.registry.ts.
#
# This file intentionally does NOT group variables under prose headers
# matching .env.example's exact wording (unreadable here -- see above);
# groupings instead follow src/config/env.ts's own inline "PHASE N --"
# comments where present, with the earliest (pre-phase-numbering) core
# variables left ungrouped at the top, matching the schema file's own
# structure.
#
# PRODUCTION-SPECIFIC REMINDERS:
#   - AWS_STORAGE_PROVIDER / STORAGE_PROVIDER: strongly recommend "s3"
#     (not "local") once you run more than one app/worker replica -- local
#     disk storage is per-container and does not survive a container
#     replacement or get shared across replicas. docker-compose.prod.yml
#     supports scaling app/worker to N replicas; local storage silently
#     breaks correctness once N > 1.
#   - Never set LLM_PROVIDER/EMBEDDING_PROVIDER to a provider whose API
#     key below is left blank -- src/config/env.ts's own Zod refinement
#     will reject startup if EMBEDDING_PROVIDER or LLM_PROVIDER is
#     "openai" without a real OPENAI_API_KEY.
# ============================================================

NODE_ENV=production  # MUST differ per environment
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@production-db-host:5432/document_ai?schema=public&connection_limit=10&pool_timeout=10  # MUST differ per environment
RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://USER:PASSWORD@production-rabbitmq-host:5672  # MUST differ per environment
REDIS_URL=redis://:PASSWORD@production-redis-host:6379  # MUST differ per environment
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://yourdomain.com  # MUST differ per environment; public base URL of this deployment
APP_URL=https://yourdomain.com  # MUST differ per environment; server-side fallback used if NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL is unset
AWS_STORAGE_PROVIDER=local
STORAGE_PROVIDER=local
# AWS_REGION=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=  # SECRET — real value only in the deploy host/CI secret store, never committed
